Source: blessh
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), @RUST@, gcc, pkgconf
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/tyetladd/blessh
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: blessh
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, bluez (>= 5.55), openssh-client, systemd
Suggests: openssh-server
Description: SSH over Bluetooth Low Energy: client and server
 blessh runs SSH over Bluetooth Low Energy, without pairing: the SSH host
 key and login provide the security. As a client, blessh lists the servers
 in range and runs the system ssh through the one chosen. As a server, it
 is off until "blessh server enable": an unprivileged daemon then registers
 a GATT service with BlueZ, listens on L2CAP connection-oriented channels
 and hands each session to a per-session "sshd -i" started by systemd
 socket activation, with the system SSH server's configuration.
